<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dētrectātor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dētract-</span></b> ),
			ōris, m.
		id.. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One who declines</i> or <i>refuses</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ministerii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 117, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A diminisher, disparager</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laudum suarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 15, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">honorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 2, 51</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
